---
description: Evidence and execution boundaries for the three-agent insights workflow
alwaysApply: true
---
Follow AGENTS.md. User intent governs the objective; never fabricate user answers.
Exploratory runs can activate from the original request after feasibility. Confirmatory
runs require explicit approval. Routine exploratory follow-ups need a recorded reason,
not repeated approval. Honor the run budget and scope exclusions.
Keep scope snapshots immutable. Preserve raw column identities in the clean base table.
Use shared calculation scripts. Read aggregate JSON previews or read_evidence.py pages;
do not print personal raw rows or inspect synthetic/.
Report descriptive patterns without manufactured p-values. Statistical nulls are scoped
to the precise metric/test. Recommendations are proposals with risks and validation plans,
not claims of causal benefit. No fixed question or insight counts; never pad a report.
